{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Implementation started in worktree peccary-fix. Design per reviewed plan: add not_a_bug AND escalated to REASON_REQUIRED_CLASSES (escalated decided reason-required — identical structural problem: no in-repo defect fixed, verifier unpassable; reason names where it was escalated to). New REPLACEMENT_SATISFIES_REASON_CLASSES={not_a_bug,escalated}: a live replacement link is checked FIRST and still short-circuits (precedence preserved); --reason is the fallback; neither present -> write-side refusal via txn.close_class_refusal naming both doors (no fall-through to the completion verifier). RED tests first in tests/unit/commands/test_close_disposition.py."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786763916834653001,"uuid":"6b3dc66f-e225-403c-9bc3-0774d33e2ac5"}